        "solution": "CREATE TABLE customers (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT, email TEXT);\nCREATE TABLE orders (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, customer_id INTEGER, total REAL, product TEXT);\n\nINSERT INTO customers VALUES (1,'Alice','a@mail.com'),(2,'Bob','b@mail.com'),(3,'Charlie','c@mail.com');\nINSERT INTO orders VALUES (1,1,250.00,'Laptop'),(2,1,45.00,'Mouse'),(3,2,180.00,'Monitor'),(4,3,75.00,'Keyboard');\n\nSELECT orders.id, customers.name, orders.product, orders.total\nFROM orders\nINNER JOIN customers ON orders.customer_id = customers.id\nWHERE orders.total > 100;",
